# Set this on the site's Vercel project, in every environment that serves
# /class. A local `npm run build` does not need it: site/vercel.ts is read
# by Vercel's build, not by Next, so a plain `next build` never evaluates
# it. Copy this file to .env.local only if you run `vercel build` locally.
#
# The site reads exactly one variable, and it is deployment wiring rather
# than application config: nothing in site/app or site/lib reads the
# environment at all. That is structural. The site is a static export
# (`output: "export"`), so it has no server and nowhere to keep a secret
# — anything set here would be inlined into the bundle at build time and
# would therefore be public. Every secret in this repo lives in the class
# app precisely because it is the half that has a server
# (research/video-calls/07-two-app-architecture.md §1).
#
# So this variable is read at *build* time, by site/vercel.ts, and never
# at request time. It is not secret; it is a public hostname.

# The class app's host for this environment, without a scheme:
# the "x" in https://x/class/... — e.g. english-learning-class.vercel.app
# for the class project's production deployment.
#
# site/vercel.ts builds the /class rewrite destination from it, which is
# what puts both apps on one domain. It is a variable rather than a
# literal in a vercel.json so that each environment can point somewhere
# different — a preview of this site at a preview of the class app, a
# production deploy at production — without editing a committed file.
#
# The build fails with a named error if this is unset, rather than
# quietly rewriting /class to https://undefined/. A scheme and any
# trailing slashes are stripped for you, so pasting the full URL out of
# the Vercel dashboard is fine.
CLASS_APP_DOMAIN=

# Three things that look as though they belong here, and do not:
#
#   Vercel Analytics and Speed Insights (@vercel/analytics,
#   @vercel/speed-insights) are zero-config on Vercel. They read the
#   deployment's own identity; there is no key to supply.
#
#   Cover images are fetched by scripts/download-covers.mjs from URLs
#   recorded in scripts/cover-images.json. No image API is called, so
#   there is no image API key.
#
#   EL_WORKFLOW_ACTIVE is not a variable to set — it is named here only
#   so that finding it in the source does not send you looking for a
#   value. scripts/workflow.mjs sets it on the child processes it spawns
#   and refuses to start when it finds it already set, which is how it
#   catches an npm script that points back at the workflow runner.
#   Setting it by hand does nothing but break workflow:dev and
#   workflow:content.

# If a variable is ever added, it belongs here — and unless it is
# genuinely public, the fact that it needs to be secret is a sign it
# belongs in the class app instead.
